What Was Found
A xss vulnerability was detected in the application.

Has This Happened Before?
Yes: 2023 Zendesk XSS via Macro Templates (CVE-2023-28109)

Security Reference: CVE-2023-28109

Why This Matters
- User-controlled content stored in database is rendered as HTML in admin context
- Attacker injects malicious script in their own profile bio
- When admin views user list, the payload executes with admin privileges
- Can steal admin session tokens, modify other user accounts, or create fake login forms
- React's dangerouslySetInnerHTML bypasses default XSS protections

Code Example (javascript)
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

// Secure sanitization utility
const sanitizeConfig = {
  ALLOWED_TAGS: ['b', 'i', 'em', 'strong', 'a', 'p', 'br'],
  ALLOWED_ATTR: ['href', 'title'],
  ALLOW_DATA_ATTR: false,
  ADD_ATTR: ['target', 'rel'],
  FORBID_TAGS: ['script', 'style', 'iframe', 'object', 'embed', 'form'],
  FORBID_ATTR: ['onerror', 'onload', 'onclick', 'onmouseover']
};

// Hook for forced attribute addition to links
DOMPurify.addHook('afterSanitizeAttributes', (node) => {
  if (node.tagName === 'A') {
    node.setAttribute('target', '_blank');
    node.setAttribute('rel', 'noopener noreferrer');
  }
});

function sanitizeUserContent(html) {
  if (!html || typeof html !== 'string') return '';
  return DOMPurify.sanitize(html, sanitizeConfig);
}

